{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Israel dwelt securely.</b> As it says: וְהָאָרֶץ שָׁקְטָה מִמִּלְחָמָה (Joshua 11:23)." "<b>Alone, the eye of Jacob — toward a land of grain and wine; indeed, the heavens shall drip dew.</b> May it be the will that the end of days produce the eye of Jacob — He is the Master whom you seek, who is the eye of Israel at the end and conclusion of all. And likewise, the heavens shall drip dew: they shall pour forth dew in abundance upon a land of grain and wine. For indeed the Messiah shall drip his teaching like dew in which all rejoice, and likewise the heavens shall pour forth dew in abundance upon a land of grain and wine, as was the state of affairs in the six days of Genesis before the sin of the first man — for it had not rained and there was no man to work the ground, but an ed would rise and water it — so that when the land is of itself a land of grain and wine, and the dripping of dew for blessing comes upon it, it suffices to sustain its inhabitants without toil, as was the intention that the first man be sustained before his sin. As the Sages said (Ketubot, last chapter): עֲתִידָה אֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁתּוֹצִיא גְּלוּסְקָאוֹת וְכֵלֵי מִילַת (The land of Israel is destined to yield ready-made cakes and fine garments)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "The phrase שֶׁלְּקֵץ הַיָּמִין is taken here as 'that the end of days produce' (לקץ הימין = end of days, with ש־ as relativizer); an alternative reading would treat it as 'of the End of Days.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:46.715893497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}